 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Not at all. It's important that bride tells her guests so they can come up plan together. A simple note on the invitation would do the trick. Then add a text message after the yes button. Say something like, Would you attend if you can't eat the bride's food? Please let me know so we can work together. No worries. Just a way to give guests a second chance after they've already committed. Some people only think about their own comfort and forget others. weddings are stress enough without food fears. If you can't eat the food, it could ruin the day for you. It' worth bringing something small from home, just in case. A few bites of your food could make a big difference. You' not. You' being thoughtful. Weddings are shared experiences, and you matter.",
